//! `rtm` binary — thin entry point. The actual policy/catalog corpus lives
//! in `src/lib.nir` (see that file's doc comment for why a `[lib]` target
//! is needed at all here). `main()` stays intentionally small: it boots the
//! binary and proves the whole corpus actually linked and registered. The
//! real guarded-read/write proof lives in `tests/guarded_ingest.rs`, and
//! serving the ~150 screens over HTTP (RFC-0022 archetype macros —
//! `login!`, `app_shell!`, `crud_screens!`, etc., all proven elsewhere in
//! this workspace) is deliberately out of scope for this pass.

fn main() {
    rtm::boot_banner();
}
